{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I will surely hide My face on that day.</b> He already mentioned above, ״והסתרתי פני מהם״ — and that was the hiding of the face of the Babylonian exile. Now the hiding of the face will return once more, and in doubled language, to let you know that this hiding will not be for a short time like the first, but they will be a long time in the hiding of the face. And it alludes to this exile of ours in which we stand in a doubled hiding of the face. But we have consolation from another place, for we stand in the assurance of (Leviticus 26:44) ״ואף גם זאת בהיותם בארץ אויביהם״. This verse reveals to us the time of the hiding, and it is the numerical value of סת״ר אסתי״ר, and its number is one thousand three hundred thirty-five, and this is what Daniel spoke at the conclusion of his vision (Daniel 12:12): ״אשרי המחכה ויגיע לימים אלף שלש מאות שלשים וחמשה״ — for then the punishment of the hiding of the face will be completed. And the verse hints to you that for so great a time the hiding will persist."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:52:41.823497109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}